{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetQUJ5SsYS4vipSFxaP5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect. I have all the information I need from the analysis. Let me summarize the key findings:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- `Order.kt:11-16` - Order entity lacks status field\n- `OrderController.kt:17-46` - Standard REST controller using ConflictException/ResourceNotFoundException\n- `OrderRepository.kt:10-27` - InMemoryOrderRepository with basic CRUD, no query-by-orderId\n- `Shipment.kt:23-27` - ShipmentStatus enum already exists (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27` - InMemoryShipmentRepository with basic CRUD, no query-by-orderId\n- `ApiError.kt:31-37` - ErrorCode enum needs new cancel-related codes\n- `GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:16-28` - Centralized exception handling\n\n**Conventions:**\n- Controllers throw ApiException subclasses; GlobalExceptionHandler transforms them to ApiError envelope\n- ErrorCode enum is the single source of truth for error codes\n- Tests use MockMvc and jsonPath to assert response bodies, not just status\n- After state-changing calls, tests issue a separate GET to verify persistence\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `Order.kt` - add status field\n2. `OrderController.kt` - add `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint\n3. `OrderRepository.kt` - add `findByOrderId` or similar to find shipments for an order\n4. `ShipmentRepository.kt` - add `findByOrderId` method\n5. `ShipmentController.kt` - add validation to reject shipments for cancelled orders\n6. `ApiError.kt` - add error codes for cancellation conflicts\n7. `OrderControllerTest.kt` - add comprehensive cancel tests\n\n**Risks:**\n- All-or-nothing atomicity: if any shipment is CONFIRMED, the entire cancel fails with no side effects\n- Idempotency: retrying a cancel on an already-cancelled order must succeed\n- Need to handle concurrent modifications safely (ConcurrentHashMap helps here)\n- Testing must verify both response and persistence (two separate assertions per case)\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** - Add `status: OrderStatus` field with enum values ACTIVE and CANCELLED. New orders default to ACTIVE.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt** - Add new method `cancel(orderId)` at `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` that:\n   - Throws 404 if order not found\n   - Throws 409 if any shipment is CONFIRMED (all-or-nothing)\n   - Succeeds (200 OK) if order is already CANCELLED (idempotent)\n   - Transitions order to CANCELLED, cancels all CREATED shipments, returns the cancelled order\n\n3. **OrderRepository.kt** - Add method `findByOrderId(orderId)` to find all shipments for an order (actually, ShipmentRepository needs this).\n\n4. **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Add `findByOrderId(orderId)` method to find all shipments for a given order.\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** - Add check in `create()` to reject shipment creation if the order is CANCELLED (409 CONFLICT).\n\n6. **ApiError.kt** - Add error codes:\n   - `ORDER_CANCELLED` - when trying to create a shipment for a cancelled order\n   - `SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED` - when trying to cancel an order that has a confirmed shipment\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt** - Add tests covering:\n   - Cancel ACTIVE order → returns CANCELLED order, persists, cancels CREATED shipments\n   - Cancel already CANCELLED order → succeeds (idempotent)\n   - Cancel with CONFIRMED shipment → 409, order stays ACTIVE, all shipments unchanged\n   - Cancel non-existent order → 404\n   - Create shipment for CANCELLED order → 409\n\n**Alternatives rejected:**\n\n- *Alternative: Use a service class for cancel logic* - The existing codebase has no service layer; logic is in controllers and repositories. Adding one would be architectural change outside scope.\n- *Alternative: Soft delete instead of status enum* - Status is explicit and queryable, matches the Shipment pattern already in use.\n- *Alternative: Add @Transactional for atomicity* - ConcurrentHashMap + single-threaded update within one method is sufficient for the in-memory fixture; adding JPA/TX would be a new dependency.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n```\nCancel ACTIVE order:\n  Input: orderId\n  1. Repository.findById(orderId) → order not found? → 404 ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n  2. Order already CANCELLED? → 200 OK, return order (idempotent)\n  3. Find all shipments for orderId via ShipmentRepository.findByOrderId()\n  4. Any shipment with status CONFIRMED? → 409 SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED, no changes made\n  5. Transition order to CANCELLED, save\n  6. Set all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED, save each\n  7. Return order (now CANCELLED) → 200 OK\n\nCreate shipment for order:\n  Input: CreateShipmentRequest with orderId\n  1. Check if order exists and is not CANCELLED\n  2. If CANCELLED → 409 ORDER_CANCELLED, no shipment created\n  3. Otherwise proceed as normal\n\nIdempotency:\n  - Cancel CANCELLED order returns 200 (not 409), order and shipments unchanged\n  - All repository updates are in-memory, no race conditions in test environment\n```\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **Cancel ACTIVE order** - POST cancel, assert 200 and CANCELLED status in response; GET order to verify persisted; verify CREATED shipments are now CANCELLED\n2. **Cancel already CANCELLED** - cancel twice, both should succeed with 200, second response should match first\n3. **Cancel blocked by CONFIRMED shipment** - create order with CONFIRMED shipment, POST cancel, assert 409 with SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED code; GET order, assert still ACTIVE; GET shipment, assert still CONFIRMED (all-or-nothing)\n4. **Cancel non-existent order** - POST cancel on non-existent ID, assert 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND code\n5. **Create shipment for CANCELLED order** - cancel order, POST shipment, assert 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED code; verify no shipment was created\n6. **Error envelope format** - verify 409 response has `error.code` and `error.message` fields\n\n---\n\nNow I'll move to implementation:\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nLet me start by modifying the Order entity to add the status field:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":896,"cache_read_input_tokens":23056,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":896},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8a33a82-1eb7-4111-9f69-ee0bc1636a93","uuid":"69ed3854-e6e3-4dd6-8c95-901394c035d6","timestamp":"2026-09-09T19:19:21.188Z","request_id":"req_011CetQUHE624hecuDh4GH6q"}
