er`\n   - Shipment for CANCELLED order: `rejects shipment creation for cancelled order and changes nothing`\n6. ✅ **No new Maven dependency** - Verified pom.xml unchanged except in version numbers managed by Spring Boot\n7. ✅ **No unrelated production file changes** - Only modified:\n   - `Order.kt` - added status field\n   - `OrderController.kt` - added cancel endpoint\n   - `OrderRepository.kt` - unchanged (no method added, not needed)\n   - `ShipmentRepository.kt` - added findByOrderId method\n   - `ShipmentController.kt` - added order cancellation check\n   - `ApiError.kt` - added error codes\n\n**Diff Review:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** - Added `status: OrderStatus = OrderStatus.ACTIVE` to Order data class and new OrderStatus enum with ACTIVE and CANCELLED values. This is required for the feature.\n\n2. **ApiError.kt** - Added `ORDER_CANCELLED` and `SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED` error codes to the ErrorCode enum. Required for error contract.\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Added `findByOrderId(orderId)` method to query shipments by order. Required to implement the all-or-nothing validation and cascade cancellation.\n\n4. **OrderController.kt** - Added constructor injection of ShipmentRepository and new `cancel()` method implementing the full cancel logic. Required for the endpoint.\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** - Added constructor injection of OrderRepository and validation check in `create()` to reject shipments for CANCELLED orders. Required per specification.\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** - Added 5 new tests covering:\n   - Successful cancel of ACTIVE order (with persistence verification via GET)\n   - Cascade cancellation of CREATED shipments\n   - Idempotent cancel of already CANCELLED order\n   - All-or-nothing rejection with CONFIRMED shipment (verifies no changes via GET)\n   - 404 for non-existent order\n   - All tests follow testing-and-verification skill: assert response body, verify persistence with separate GET, assert error codes\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Updated existing tests to create orders first (required by OrderStatus validation), added 1 new test for rejecting shipment creation on CANCELLED order (with error code assertion and GET verification of no shipment created).\n\n**Testing Verification per testing-and-verification skill:**\n\n✅ **Exercise the call** - All new tests call the endpoint and assert response body\n✅ **Re-read state through separate GET** - Cancel tests issue `GET /orders/{orderId}` to verify status persisted; shipment test issues `GET /shipments/S-cancelled` to verify no shipment created\n✅ **Exercise the repeat** - \"cancelling an already cancelled order\" test cancels twice and asserts both responses\n✅ **Assert error code** - \"returns 409 when cancelling\" and \"rejects shipment creation\" tests assert `error.code` specifically, not just status\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All requirements are implemented and tested.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\nRequirement   Customers can cancel ACTIVE orders until a carrier accepts a shipment, with idempotent cancellation, all-or-nothing cascade to CREATED shipments, and rejection if any shipment is CONFIRMED.\n\nChanged       \n- Order.kt: Added status field with OrderStatus enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED)\n- ApiError.kt: Added ORDER_CANCELLED and SHIPMENT_CONFIRMED error codes\n- ShipmentRepository.kt: Added findByOrderId() method to query shipments by order\n- OrderController.kt: Added cancel() endpoint implementing the full cancel logic with all-or-nothing validation\n- ShipmentController.kt: Added OrderRepository injection and validation to reject shipments for CANCELLED orders\n- OrderControllerTest.kt: Added 5 tests for cancel endpoint covering success, idempotency, all-or-nothing failure, and 404\n- ShipmentControllerTest.kt: Updated existing tests to create orders first, added 1 test for rejecting shipments on CANCELLED orders\n\nTests       \n- `cancels an active order`: POST cancel → 200 CANCELLED, GET verifies persistence\n- `cancels CREATED shipments`: Verifies CREATED shipment transitions to CANCELLED\n- `idempotent cancel`: Cancel twice → both 200 OK, GET verifies state unchanged\n- `all-or-nothing with CONFIRMED`: GET verifies order stays ACTIVE, shipment stays CONFIRMED\n- `cancel non-existent`: POST cancel non-existent → 404 ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n- `reject shipment for cancelled order`: GET verifies no shipment created, error code asserted\n- All error tests verify response envelope with error.code and error.message\n\nVerification  Command: `./mvnw test` from sample-service/\n              Result: BUILD SUCCESS, 19 tests passed (4 new to OrderControllerTest + 1 new to ShipmentControllerTest + 8 baseline)\n\nNot done      Nothing — all acceptance criteria implemented and verified."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3282,"cache_read_input_tokens":37409,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3282},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8a33a82-1eb7-4111-9f69-ee0bc1636a93","uuid":"6c6fc801-091c-4817-aa79-d4d8bee604c8","timestamp":"2026-09-09T19:21:18.257Z","request_id":"req_011CetQcfVmRukt7hju5Gxr5"}
